ukui-settings-daemon: let the compositor gamma-manager own brightness on sheng

On the Xiaomi Pad 6S Pro (sheng) the panel exposes
/sys/class/backlight/ktz8866-backlight but openKylin's upm cannot drive it
(org.ukui.powermanagement -> CanSetBrightness == false), so
UsdBaseClass::upmSupportAdjustBrightness() -- which only checks for the
existence of a backlight node -- returns true.  The compositor gamma-manager
(GmHelper) then treats the first (and only) output as a "notebook internal
panel" and pegs its brightness to 100 on every screen reconfiguration
(GmHelper::updateWlcomOutputInfo and friends), so the user's brightness is lost
on screen rotation and at session start.

Fix: make the hardware-backlight path own brightness only when upm can actually
set it.  Otherwise the gamma-manager (which persists brightness in
/etc/ukui/usd/globalconf.ini, section [color]) owns the screen brightness, and
it is preserved across rotation / reboot.

Equivalent live/build change: tools/sheng-usd-brightness-fix.sh patches the
compiled copies of this function (daemon binary + every plugin .so).

--- a/common/usd_base_class.cpp
+++ b/common/usd_base_class.cpp
@@ -1326,6 +1326,24 @@ bool UsdBaseClass::upmSupportAdjustBrightness()
     static int ret = -1;
     if (ret > -1) return ret;
     ret = 0;
+
+    // [sheng] The hardware backlight only owns brightness when the
+    // power-management service can actually drive it. On the sheng tablet the
+    // panel exposes /sys/class/backlight/ktz8866-backlight but upm reports
+    // CanSetBrightness == false, so the compositor gamma-manager MUST own the
+    // brightness. Otherwise the gamma-manager treats the first (and only)
+    // output as a notebook "internal panel" and pegs it to 100 on every screen
+    // reconfiguration (rotation), dropping the user's brightness to maximum.
+    // See GmHelper::updateWlcomOutputInfo().
+    QDBusInterface powerInterface("org.ukui.powermanagement",
+                                  "/",
+                                  "org.ukui.powermanagement.interface",
+                                  QDBusConnection::systemBus());
+    QDBusReply<bool> setable = powerInterface.call("CanSetBrightness");
+    if (setable.isValid() && !setable.value()) {
+        return ret; // 0 -> compositor gamma-manager owns brightness
+    }
+
     QDir brightnessNodeDir(BRIGHTNESS_NODE_PATH);
     QStringList nodeDirs = brightnessNodeDir.entryList(QDir::Dirs | QDir::NoDotAndDotDot);
 
